---
title: "Refund Policy — OnlinePDFPro"
description: "Refund policy for digital products purchased on OnlinePDFPro."

permalink: /refund.html
bodyClass: hp-body
---
{% extends "base.njk" %}
{% block head %}
<style>
.legal-page { max-width: 740px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 24px 80px; }
.legal-heading { font-family: var(--hp-serif, 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.legal-heading em { font-style: italic; }
.legal-updated { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--hp-text-muted, #706558); margin-bottom: 40px; }
.legal-section { margin-bottom: 32px; }
.legal-section h2 { font-family: var(--hp-serif, 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif); font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px; }
.legal-section p, .legal-section li { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--hp-text-secondary, #6b5e4f); line-height: 1.7; }
.legal-section ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 8px 0; }
.legal-section li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
.legal-contact { background: var(--hp-bg-alt, #efe9de); padding: 24px; margin-top: 40px; }
.legal-contact p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--hp-text-secondary, #6b5e4f); line-height: 1.7; }
.legal-contact a { color: var(--hp-accent, #8b6914); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="legal-page">
    <h1 class="legal-heading">Refund <em>Policy</em></h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: August 2026</p>

    <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Digital Products</h2>
        <p>All study materials sold on OnlinePDFPro are digital products (PDF files) delivered instantly upon purchase. Due to the nature of digital goods, all sales are generally final.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>When We Issue Refunds</h2>
        <p>We will issue a full refund in the following circumstances:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>You were charged but did not receive the product</li>
            <li>The product is significantly different from its description</li>
            <li>The PDF file is corrupted or cannot be opened</li>
            <li>You were charged multiple times for the same product</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Refund Request Process</h2>
        <p>To request a refund, email <a href="mailto:support@onlinepdfpro.com" style="color:var(--hp-accent);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">support@onlinepdfpro.com</a> within 7 days of purchase with:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Your order ID or payment reference</li>
            <li>The email address used for purchase</li>
            <li>A brief description of the issue</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We aim to process refund requests within 3–5 business days.</p>
        <p>If you are signed in, your purchase information is available in <a href="/library.html" style="color:var(--hp-accent);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">My Library</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Non-Refundable Cases</h2>
        <p>Refunds will not be issued if:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>You simply changed your mind after purchase</li>
            <li>You have already downloaded and used the product</li>
            <li>The request is made more than 7 days after purchase</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Free PDF Tools</h2>
        <p>Our free PDF tools (merge, compress, split, etc.) are provided at no cost. No payment is involved and therefore no refund applies.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-contact">
        <p>Questions about refunds? Contact us at <a href="mailto:support@onlinepdfpro.com">support@onlinepdfpro.com</a></p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
